# RavinSec — Marketing Site Standards

**Representation site only** — not a product suite. Showcase RavinSec services with a clean, modern, CMS-driven experience.

## Scope

| In scope | Out of scope |
|----------|----------------|
| Marketing pages, services overview | Dashboards, SaaS billing, real-time feeds |
| **Blog / weblog**, **news**, **contact** | Auth portals, RBAC apps, NOC/SOC tools |
| CMS-managed content | Heavy 3D, attack simulators, live threat maps |

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Choices |
|-------|---------|
| Framework | Next.js 14+ App Router, TypeScript |
| UI | **shadcn/ui** + Tailwind CSS (dark default) |
| Motion | Framer Motion — subtle page/section transitions only |
| CMS | **Payload CMS** (open source, self-hosted) — **content lives in CMS, not hardcoded** |
| Forms | react-hook-form + zod; contact via Route Handler + Resend (or similar) |
| Images | `next/image`; CMS image URLs via loader when needed |
| SEO | Metadata API, sitemap, Open Graph |
| Hosting | Vercel |

Prefer **shadcn components** (`Button`, `Card`, `NavigationMenu`, `Form`, etc.) over custom primitives. Add via CLI; extend in `components/ui/`.

## Agentic Workflow

**Before:** Read existing patterns → short plan for non-trivial work → wait for approval when scope is unclear.

**During:** Keep diffs small; match project conventions; validate contact/form input server-side.

**After:** Check responsive layout, accessibility, and Lighthouse basics.

## Security (lightweight)

- Validate/sanitize contact form input (zod + server handler)
- Rate-limit contact API; optional Turnstile on contact form
- No secrets in client bundles; env vars for CMS tokens and email API

## Code Style

- Functional components; strict TypeScript
- `components/ui/` — shadcn; `components/sections/` — page blocks; `components/layout/` — header/footer
- Mobile-first; dark mode; professional security aesthetic (clean, not flashy)

## File Layout

```
src/
├── app/
│   ├── (site)/          # pages: home, services, about
│   ├── blog/            # weblog listing + [slug]
│   ├── news/            # news listing + [slug]
│   ├── contact/
│   └── api/contact/
├── components/ui|sections|layout/
├── lib/cms.ts|utils.ts
└── content/             # only if using local MDX fallback
```

## Context Rules

Use `@cms` when editing content models, fetchers, or blog/news pages.

## Success Criteria

Clear messaging, fast pages, editable content in CMS, polished shadcn UI, working contact flow.
